<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">User Agency vs. System Constraints</strong>: Your action shows agency within a system that prioritizes viral metrics. Similarly, Hanson tries to assert pragmatic goals (futarchy) within a media ecosystem that rewards clickbait, illustrating the tension between individual intent and structural incentives.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Behavioral Signaling</strong>: Hansonâ€™s work on signaling \citep{hanson2009} could frame your "like" as a signalâ€”not of approval, but of personal tracking. This underscores how platform interactions often serve hidden motives, a theme central to Hansonâ€™s intellectual project.</li>
