<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Robin Hanson has a bold idea: <a href="https://www.econtalk.org/robin-hanson-on-futarchy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">futarchy</a>, where voters set goalsâ€”like boosting prosperity or cutting inequalityâ€”and prediction markets pick the best policies <a href="https://doi.org/10.1111/1467-9760.00128" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"></a>. Itâ€™s practical and testable. So why is he known for <a href="https://grabbyaliens.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">â€œgrabby aliensâ€</a> and sexbots?</p>
